/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  Reporting-Endpoints: csp-endpoint="https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report"
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://api.cireweddings.com http://localhost:8787; connect-src 'self' https://api.cireweddings.com http://localhost:8787; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; report-uri https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report; report-to csp-endpoint

# The organiser portal is a STATIC Astro build on Cloudflare Pages, so the asset
# layer serves every response and this file covers all of them. (The guest site
# can't do that — it's an SSR Worker, which is why cire/web carries the same
# policy in `src/lib/security-headers.ts` middleware as well. Nothing here needs
# a middleware twin.)
#
# TWO POLICIES ON PURPOSE:
#
# 1. The ENFORCED line carries only directives that cannot break a working page:
#    the portal has no `<object>`/`<embed>` and no `<base>`, and must never be
#    framed (it holds a session cookie for the whole account and full guest
#    lists). `X-Frame-Options` above is the legacy twin of `frame-ancestors`.
#
# 2. The REPORT-ONLY line is the real lock-down, staged the same way cire/web
#    staged its own (S-L1): it reports to the first-party collector
#    (`POST /api/csp-report` on cire-api — public, creds-less, 204-always) so a
#    directive that is subtly too tight shows up as a violation report instead
#    of a broken portal. Flip the header name to `Content-Security-Policy` once
#    a real-browser pass over sign-in, the invite builder, image cropping and
#    the CSV export produces no reports.
#
# WHY EACH SOURCE IS THERE (audited against the portal's source, not guessed):
#
#   script-src 'unsafe-inline'  The theme-boot script (`THEME_BOOT_SCRIPT`, both
#                               page shells) is `is:inline` so it runs before
#                               first paint and can't be a hashed external file.
#                               Astro's island bootstrap is external `/_astro/*`
#                               and covered by 'self'.
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'   Astro inlines small critical CSS; Solid writes
#                               `style={{…}}` attributes (hence style-src-attr).
#   font-src 'self'             Schibsted Grotesk + Cormorant Garamond are
#                               SELF-HOSTED — `astro.config.mjs` downloads them
#                               at build time via `fontProviders.google()`. No
#                               fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com, unlike
#                               cire/web, which still links the stylesheet.
#   img-src data: blob:         `data:` for the cropperjs canvas, `blob:` for
#                               it and for `lib/download.ts`'s object URLs.
#   img-src api.cireweddings…   Every uploaded image (invite art, event photos)
#                               is served by cire-api. NB: a profile avatar can
#                               arrive from the OIDC `picture` claim pointing at
#                               ANY https host — OSN has no avatar hosting yet,
#                               so nothing populates it today and no origin is
#                               allowlisted. Add the host here when it exists;
#                               until then a set avatar renders empty rather
#                               than falling back to the initial.
#   connect-src                 cire-api only. Sign-in is a TOP-LEVEL redirect
#                               to musubi, not a fetch, and a navigation is not
#                               a connect-src subject — so the OSN origin is
#                               deliberately absent. The localhost entry keeps a
#                               local `wrangler pages dev dist` working against
#                               a local API without loosening production.
#   frame-src / worker-src      The portal embeds no iframes (Maps and Pinterest
#                               appear only as `href` links) and spawns no
#                               workers. 'none' both.
